---
source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: the run order for flake.safix.users.alice carries a cycle of generators:
'base' -> 'derived' -> 'base'. Nothing can run first, so nothing runs.

Nothing was written. The order is flake.safix.lib.generatorPlan's and
this runtime derives none of its own: a cycle is refused at evaluation,
and the generators inside one are left out of the order rather than
placed in it. An order carrying one therefore did not come from that
refusal — a stand-in for nix, or a program that built the plan itself.

Refused before the first generator rather than at the one that cannot
read its input, because this command commits each generator as it goes: a
cycle met part-way through a run has already committed values and cannot
finish, and a committed value is a distributed one.
